is not sampling-completion rate; accepted records may be a smaller subset.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 8]\nThe scientific sequence begins with this relationship: Each station travels through distinct state transitions.\nThe connected effect is described by A missing signed record cannot be counted as sampled.\nA monitoring project progresses through planned, access-ready, collected, laboratory received and QC accepted statuses. Each requires different documentary proof and may be tracked by different owners.\nReadiness ratio is not sampling-completion rate; accepted records may be a smaller subset.\nThis separates a visible scientific response from the further testing needed for a real operational conclusion.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 9]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 1  /  SOURCE RECORD\nRAREMINDS\nRead the values before calculating anything\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n9\nILLUSTRATIVE INPUTS — TAUGHT EXAMPLE\nPlan3 sites; access approved for2; actual signed collection at1.\nWORK STEP 1\nReadiness=2/3×100=66.7%.\nWORK STEP 2\nSampling completion=1/3×100=33.3%; QC accepted=1/3×100=33.3% if that one accepted.\nWORK STEP 3\nDo not merge access clearance, collection and QC stages.\nBefore a real report is accepted, sample ID, date, method, unit and quality status must be checked.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 9]\nThe given teaching inputs are Plan3 sites; access approved for2; actual signed collection at1.\nThe first working relationship is Readiness=2/3×100=66.7%.\nThe next calculation or interpretation is sampling completion=1/3×100=33.3%; QC accepted=1/3×100=33.3% if that one accepted.\nThe inputs and calculated steps are distinct. These figures are not presented as readings taken from a specific certified instrument.\nA field or laboratory report would additionally require an identifiable sample, method, date, units and quality status.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 10]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 1  /  FORMULA & VARIABLES\nRAREMINDS\nBuild the scientific relationship from its parts\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n10\n","embedding":"[-0.004292885,0.019045277,0.0020741124,-0.029988613,-0.0233858,-0.04109444,-0.00627656,-0.039918806,-0.00038851492,-0.058863632,0.008452283,0.005999755,-0.003989943,0.027016746,-0.018434804,-0.002838813,0.0038669116,-0.0056568906,-0.004899539,-0.012793447,0.0028487288,-0.006775424,-0.015337384,0.048727162,-0.033007693,0.022331093,0.028972983,-0.011597838,-0.028686265,0.0837639,0.0071610017,-0.030493975,-0.02363862,0.010368876,0.015323184,0.005730737,-0.0068630506,0.0056978157,0.031224666,0.025040563,0.0047407574,-0.045440257,0.025845576,-0.010627947,-0.010518406,0.0003498408,0.015631802,0.012940735,-0.03122434,0.01742975,-0.012727925,-0.0014208424,0.029127741,-0.003680484,-0.006187977,-0.01240232,-0.017773865,0.0294994,0.027110482,0.02685244,-0.023097102,-0.0032578541,0.0341536,0.014863375,0.014022752,-0.013082024,0.022877747,-0.03052174,0.008386049,0.030793212,0.03149338,0.009501217,-0.032913834,-0.0051161344,-0.030581674,-0.04783666,-0.06886472,0.028818017,-0.031725597,0.017332027,-0.012502534,-0.024858408,-0.01882393,0.009815328,-0.022850214,0.009883021,-0.03481106,0.0007456726,0.023041008,0.028202187,0.015993176,-0.025899634,-0.00028542118,-0.016707886,-0.021317074,-0.002227162,0.04199026,-0.013968933,-0.018655822,-0.04397757,-0.026315043,0.02199998,0.0063740364,0.004411739,0.0131779155,-0.029997835,-0.04047772,0.03578239,-0.0017317393,0.01048749,-0.036901936,-0.16598642,0.007095249,0.016939254,-0.021453422,0.10007334,0.047641825,0.028279953,-0.018934399,0.016638588,0.00