7, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 59]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  WORKING METHOD\nRAREMINDS\nFollow the process: input → action → observed result\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n59\n1\nSOURCE\nApproval, commitment, invoice and payment are distinct states; closure requires evidence of completed authorised verification.\n2\nOPERATION\n3\nCHECK\nA numeric budget remainder is not cash spent or available for purchasing without approvals.\nVISIBLE RESULT / CAUTION: A numeric budget remainder is not cash spent or available for purchasing without approvals.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 59]\nThe scientific sequence begins with this relationship: Approval, commitment, invoice and payment are distinct states; closure requires evidence of completed authorised verification.\nFinancial control distinguishes planned estimates, conditional authority, purchase commitments, invoices and payments. Each status needs its own dated evidence; closure is a separate professional decision.\nA numeric budget remainder is not cash spent or available for purchasing without approvals.\nThis separates a visible scientific response from the further testing needed for a real operational conclusion.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 60]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  SOURCE RECORD\nRAREMINDS\nRead the values before calculating anything\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n60\nILLUSTRATIVE INPUTS — TAUGHT EXAMPLE\nPlanned₹85,900\nWORK STEP 1\nconditional₹65,100\nWORK STEP 2\noutside conditional₹20,800\nWORK STEP 3\nactual paid UNKNOWN until vouchers/ledger exist\nBefore a real report is accepted, sample ID, date, method, un