14008,-0.025426941,-0.050784294,0.0056270994,0.039775085,-0.011698655,-0.00806183,0.006819546,-0.020922402,0.03647858,0.0048164744,0.013761774,0.0263317,-0.01936172,0.019920459,0.010308407,-0.02256967,0.004966078,0.036424488,0.016305653,0.0162402,0.018203948,0.023150373,-0.009343086,-0.0024897098,-0.012457053,-0.021636333,-0.0526227,-0.027366841,0.001261469,0.0032033394,0.01885699,0.024555612,0.027095476,0.0015838904,-0.0064504268,-0.007133813,-0.004462888,-0.0017607957,-0.0019678366,-0.0058665327,0.03705792,-0.021646356,-0.010566762,-0.0156316,-0.0005777434,-0.0064592687,0.007776257,-0.046019796,-0.0023854643]","token_count":1044,"source_location":{"name":"Course 15 — Environmental Monitoring, Risk and Engineering Decisions (with speaker notes).pptx","limitations":"Extracted slide XML text, table cell text and speaker notes. Images, diagrams, charts and embedded media are not visually interpreted; layouts are flattened.","extracted_end":31422,"extracted_start":28291},"created_at":"2026-11-18T08:06:14.435833+00:00"},{"id":"2b1a76b0-d276-4e50-8808-a9994fb114e2","analysis_id":"47ea0217-a6c9-4726-984b-c2e788d4a5b7","chunk_index":29,"content":"erty or situation.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 66]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 4  /  ERROR ANALYSIS\nRAREMINDS\nFind the wrong reasoning and repair it\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n66\nINCORRECT OR MISLEADING CLAIM\nApplying an enclosed-pipe threshold unchanged to natural river flow.\nWHAT THE TAUGHT EVIDENCE REALLY SUPPORTS\nOpen-channel river classification requires hydraulic radius and often Froude number; Re threshold differs.  A smooth-looking river surface is not proof that the water column is laminar.\nWHY THE ERROR MATTERS\nUse fit-for-geometry turbulence model and measured conditions\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 66]\nThe incorrect claim is applying an enclosed-pipe threshold unchanged to natural river flow.\nOpen-channel river classification requires hydraulic radius and often Froude number; Re threshold differs. A smooth-looking river surface is not proof that the water column is laminar.\nThe error matters because it ignores this boundary: use fit-for-geometry turbulence model and measured conditions.\nThe correction rests on the actual evidence and model, rather than on a rule remembered without its conditions.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 67]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 4  /  ACADEMIC GLOSSARY\nRAREMINDS\nRelated words and their precise meanings\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n67\nρ\ndensity\nμ\ndynamic viscosity\nD or Dh\nhydraulic diameter\nRe\ndimensionless inertial/viscous ratio\nReynolds number\ninertial/viscous ratio\nTransition\nregime sensitive to disturbances\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 67]\nThe term ρ means density.\nThe term μ means dynamic viscosity.\nThe term D or Dh means hydraulic diameter.\nThe term Re means dimensionless inertial/viscous ratio.\nThe term Reynolds number means inertial/viscous ratio.\nThe term Transition means regime sensitive to disturbances.\nThese definitions belong together because the model uses more than one quantity, structure or process. The words are precise scientific terms, not interchangeable labels.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 68]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 4  /  APPLY INDEPENDENTLY\nRAREMINDS\nNew case — answer before opening t