61609+00:00"},{"id":"2f5ada74-7b01-4bb5-92f7-d0e2e8e1aad1","analysis_id":"61b722f5-8838-4257-8470-376c62f24aa4","chunk_index":25,"content":"llustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 56]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  DEFINITIONS & COMPONENTS\nRAREMINDS\nEvery part, symbol and meaning\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n56\nPlanned\nforecast cost\nConditional\nauthorised planning scope with conditions\nCommitted\nvalid PO/contract\nInvoiced\nbilled amount\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 56]\nThe term Planned refers to forecast cost.\nThe term Conditional refers to authorised planning scope with conditions.\nThe term Committed refers to valid PO/contract.\nThe term Invoiced refers to billed amount.\nThese terms describe different parts of the same scientific relationship. Treating them as interchangeable would obscure what the equipment measures or what the formula actually calculates.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 57]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  MECHANISM\nRAREMINDS\nWhat physically or chemically changes?\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n57\n1\nApproval, commitment, invoice and payment are distinct states; closure requires evidence of completed authorised verification.\nWHY THIS HAPPENS\nFinancial control distinguishes planned estimates, conditional authority, purchase commitments, invoices and payments. Each status needs its own dated evidence; closure is a separate professional decision.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 57]\nFirst, approval, commitment, invoice and payment are distinct states; closure requires evidence of completed authorised verification.\nThe sequence is a scientific explanation: the visible outcome follows from the preceding conditions, rather than appearing as an unexplained result.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 58]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  APPARATUS & OBSERVATION\nRAREMINDS\nConnect the science to real equipment and evidence\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n58\nRECONSTRUCTED TEACHING SCENE  •  NOT AUTHENTICATED FIELD FOOTAGE\nWHAT THE LEARNER MUST OBSERVE\nFive-state ledger with blank/unknown transaction values, not fabricated zeros.\nHOW THE EVIDENCE IS PRODUCED\nA ledger should preserve blanks or UNKNOWN for transactions without supporting records, with explicit references to conditional approval and closure gate.\nUse authentic method, equipment ID, calibration record and signed observations for a real laboratory result.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 58]\nFive-state ledger with blank/unknown transaction values, not fabricated zeros.\nA ledger should preserve blanks or UNKNOWN for transactions without supporting records, with explicit references to conditional approval and closure gate.\nThe pictured setup illustrates the relevant equipment or model. It is not authenticated footage from a completed measurement.\n","embedding":"[0.01003901,0.005362086,0.021176664,-0.025380205,-0.0066321925,-0.025211265,-0.012385854,-0.045310397,0.012762855,-0.08219261,0.0038778002,0.006569858,0.0013464052,0.008872493,-0.0064970674,-0.009985967,-0.011657537,-0.016626345,-0.0004494714,-0.003374436,-0.016179953,-0.010104643,-0.026223168,0.011167578,-0.045612767,0.016976805,0.017564641,-0.022423109,-0.01652379,0.107256204,-0.005950403,-0.01704895,-0.0065228823,-0.0031158486,0.012050263,-0.0071641863,0.0026141158,0.01465149,0.030386003,0.025432874,0.010230771,-0.03938226,0.027056914,0.0033869324,-0.009631061,0.001986342,-0.0022195526,0.012038251,-0.026691582,0.012280757,0.0026115736,0.00