://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 47]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  SCIENTIFIC VISUAL\nRAREMINDS\nConnect the measured evidence to the mechanism\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n47\nREAD THE VISUAL\nThis is a constructed teaching dataset. Read the axes, units, input assumptions and shape before interpreting any trend or difference.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 47]\nA pump adds mechanical energy to fluid. The system requires static elevation head plus pipe friction and fittings; the pump supplies decreasing head with increasing flow. Their curve intersection determines a feasible operating point under assumptions.\nThe diagram, chart or labelled schematic makes the scientific relationship visible, while the accompanying words identify the conditions being represented.\nThe illustration should not be mistaken for a calibrated field or laboratory observation.\nIts value is in connecting a mechanism to an observation or calculation; claims beyond that need additional data.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 48]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  INTERPRETATION\nRAREMINDS\nWhat is supported — and what is not?\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n48\nSUPPORTED SCIENTIFIC MEANING\nThe hydraulic power is 2.94kW, smaller than required electrical input.  The lowest-power numerical option is not necessarily an operable pump at the required head.\nCOMMON OVERCLAIM\nSizing motor from hydraulic power alone\nPROFESSIONAL BOUNDARY\nRated pump curves, NPSH and electrical safety approval required\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 48]\nThe hydraulic power is 2.94kW, smaller than required electrical input. The lowest-power numerical option is not necessarily an operable pump at the required head.\nA possible overclaim would be sizing motor from hydraulic power alone.\nThe professional limit is rated pump curves, NPSH and electrical safety approval required.\nA defensible conclusion says what the evidence establishes and does not silently extend it to an untested property or situation.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 49]\n","embedding":"[0.0038549302,0.008313629,0.00037415166,0.0017454794,-0.004894191,-0.029862693,0.015306056,-0.04468106,-0.006283011,-0.08074369,0.024974901,0.01281493,0.012096527,-0.0013330601,0.0071403338,-0.025136895,0.0051742434,-0.021061,-0.010765255,-0.0078661945,0.0098911,-0.0016239668,-0.0049980893,0.039302543,-0.07371785,0.02986198,0.03716674,-0.015445743,-0.03980423,0.10011535,-0.01367592,-0.014308288,-0.023186127,-0.009456524,0.01924699,0.0173682,0.011666502,-0.02141502,0.0040537585,0.0017104679,0.01810167,-0.0164313,-0.009025644,0.010595207,0.011338015,0.025047498,-0.0067926003,0.039956216,-0.004892053,-0.0049558,-0.014523434,-0.0034122902,0.01287165,-0.018274182,0.0010875004,0.0030661083,-0.029973853,0.03420476,0.04997117,0.0069174427,-0.006746476,-0.0076050153,0.03836487,0.0019820374,0.0006286321,-0.00973988,0.016419096,-0.016137363,0.019252347,0.023012739,-0.0020865696,-0.018562123,-0.015033971,0.0021238613,-0.012632004,-0.03306203,-0.06104664,0.00591498,-0.033054218,0.019453602,0.01019396,-0.027806705,-0.023598647,0.010203582,-0.04404529,0.025478875,-0.031164486,-0.021045508,0.029247208,0.039819703,0.010205019,-0.014526653,-0.0007113774,-0.028072096,-0.0141740395,-0.0073802467,0.032561883,-0.036141485,-0.0044924426,-0.018190274,-0.041418128,-0.0005166027,0.0292279,0.0018543926,0.0014872905,-0.03027517,-0.019034492,0.0052647535,-0.014764162,0.002864526,-0.033779245,-0.18892518,0.0121064335,0.