0.0044648093,0.012687871,0.013635743,-0.0057215346,0.018590372,0.0073442524,0.0055270875,-0.001280164,-0.00079613406,0.006366247,-0.008960704,-0.0032316253,0.012893379,-0.006029019,-0.013811191,-0.0041236333,-0.00928886,-0.003735338,0.033005837,-0.013668175,-0.009841366]","token_count":1056,"source_location":{"name":"Course 04 — Fluid Mechanics and River Hydraulics (with speaker notes).pptx","limitations":"Extracted slide XML text, table cell text and speaker notes. Images, diagrams, charts and embedded media are not visually interpreted; layouts are flattened.","extracted_end":20196,"extracted_start":17028},"created_at":"2026-11-18T08:06:29.161609+00:00"},{"id":"6317ce1f-de8f-48e6-9c82-8ca4553abd2b","analysis_id":"47ea0217-a6c9-4726-984b-c2e788d4a5b7","chunk_index":21,"content":"ce establishes and does not silently extend it to an untested property or situation.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 49]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  ERROR ANALYSIS\nRAREMINDS\nFind the wrong reasoning and repair it\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n49\nINCORRECT OR MISLEADING CLAIM\nSizing electrical supply from hydraulic power only.\nWHAT THE TAUGHT EVIDENCE REALLY SUPPORTS\nThe hydraulic power is 2.94kW, smaller than required electrical input.  The lowest-power numerical option is not necessarily an operable pump at the required head.\nWHY THE ERROR MATTERS\nRated pump curves, NPSH and electrical safety approval required\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 49]\nThe incorrect claim is sizing electrical supply from hydraulic power only.\nThe hydraulic power is 2.94kW, smaller than required electrical input. The lowest-power numerical option is not necessarily an operable pump at the required head.\nThe error matters because it ignores this boundary: rated pump curves, NPSH and electrical safety approval required.\nThe correction rests on the actual evidence and model, rather than on a rule remembered without its conditions.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 50]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  ACADEMIC GLOSSARY\nRAREMINDS\nRelated words and their precise meanings\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n50\nStatic head\nelevation difference\nFriction head\nflow-dependent loss\nPump curve\nhead versus Q\nMotor efficiency\nelectrical to shaft\nTotal dynamic head\nstatic + loss head\nPump efficiency\nhydraulic output over shaft input\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 50]\nThe term Static head means elevation difference.\nThe term Friction head means flow-dependent loss.\nThe term Pump curve means head versus Q.\nThe term Motor efficiency means electrical to shaft.\nThe term Total dynamic head means static + loss head.\nThe term Pump efficiency means hydraulic output over shaft input.\nThese definitions belong together because the model uses more than one quantity, structure or process. The words are precise scientific terms, not interchangeable labels.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 51]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  APPLY INDEPENDENTLY\nRAREMINDS\nNew case — answer before opening the next slide\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n51\nNEW SOURCE RECORD\nWater Q=0.010 m³/s; total head H=20 m; pump efficiency 0.65; motor efficiency 0.90\nYOUR SCIENTIFIC QUESTION\nCompute hydraulic and required electrical power.\nWHAT TO SHOW IN YOUR ANSWER\n","embedding":"[0.008562424,0.0101312725,0.0032213149,0.0001342617,-0.013466637,-0.021963136,0.015735416,-0.06089353,-0.0076462245,-0.08501434,0.012577193,0.027456162,0.03142543,0.0025491228,-0.009787334,-0.018231204,0.021956606,-0.025687218,-0.00075975934,-0.010495283,0.0055096042,-0.018343361,0.018936826,0.016823519,-0.056369506,0.013429911,0.020823162,-0.011872737,-0.020690816,0.09772275,-0.0137040485,-0.008618663,-0.019142961,-0.01663089,0.010093157,0.030375239,-0.00033739556,0.002214471,2.7135382e-06,0.011141967,0.0024541381,-0.01872683,-0.0026322776,0.0041847965,0.011765605,0.009874076,-0.012967376,0.039425056,-0.014430222,-0.00021547455,-0.011869065,-0.012908477,0.020052107,-0.0035280294,0.0068011396,0.004815314,-0.033081394,0.0401299,0.048948012,-0.0006775681,-0.004988696,0.008619003,0.030335011,0.011256707,-0.008205369,-0.0140922,0.031510532,-0.027618945,0.024375366,0.01723353,-0.0013452086,-0.0077386247,-0.018951098,-0.0051210145,-0.01685118,-0.05340838,-0.07023133,-0.0020169036,-0.030002527,0.028937114,-0.010187368,-0.02605587,-0.02078837,-0.0021530031,-0.049214482,0.028990244,-0.030726492,-0.013965524,0.020750059,0.021152211,0.003862084,-0.013799117,0.00049092725,-0.032290246,-0.009127614,-0.016694069,0.029758686,-0.017264478,-0.00010668126,-0.024195207,-0.029015835,-0.008798409,0.042504124,-0.005808331,0.0041035833,-0.050012212,-0.0018714315,0.004772992,-0.026239982,0.018097287,-0.02842337,-0.19825777,0.001356542,0.010335284,-0.03432219,0.031530306,0.02957507,0.037000217,-0.009732351,-0.010820244,0.011441407,0.008769388,-0.010341524,-0.01781207,-0.024121212,0.001844642,0.011245511,-0.011698837,-0.030808918,0.02989738,0.032370847,0.034029063,-0.009067362,0.023454716,0.017468601,0.0051683513,0.02649979,0.013119465,-0.0013677585,-0.03379456,0.016022896,-0.043208912,0.001043473,-0.024958234,-0.022591656,-0.019024504,0.0057680313,-0.02509723,0.019289048,-0.022860168,-0.009832587,0.019010251,0.005012497,0.011011213,0.023962637,0.00615728