n headings.\n2\nExplain what changes in the scientific system and why.\n3\nRead a source record and identify units, assumptions and QC gaps.\n4\nCalculate a new example, including intermediate steps and checks.\n5\nExplain what is supported, what is unknown and who can approve.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 72]\nCompletion means being able to explain an idea in ordinary scientific language, not merely repeat a definition or formula.\nA sound answer identifies the evidence, names the relevant units, uses the appropriate model, and shows how the result follows from the given values.\nIt also separates an observation from an interpretation and identifies assumptions or missing quality checks.\nProfessional authorisation is separate from succeeding in an illustrative academic calculation.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1","embedding":"[0.004168033,0.03218438,-0.018658694,0.020917317,0.006810421,-0.019369958,-0.0051452024,-0.0602864,0.012589034,-0.089074366,0.009123274,0.03752381,0.025362946,0.015868641,-0.001119091,-0.007893866,0.018762957,-0.031022094,-0.021945639,-0.01080373,0.0071792877,-0.028202254,-0.024337096,0.042766266,-0.053774625,0.005551821,0.02153551,-0.024672689,-0.0229279,0.14037308,-0.018859243,-0.03304924,0.008830384,0.00021264076,0.008318717,0.0154685555,0.008535612,0.00022343869,0.021656316,0.019823845,0.017922198,-0.035795346,-0.0121581135,0.008589784,-0.021110274,0.0055225394,-0.011286059,0.0009788251,-0.007902401,0.006176633,0.0018961208,0.016714882,-0.014190112,-0.02594879,0.012717753,-0.0016725851,-0.025073469,0.03591866,0.040900543,0.03607674,0.002498885,0.0001515429,0.039108343,0.033040658,0.026834905,-0.004006548,0.036468316,-0.039173152,0.013813005,-0.010987359,0.0022205487,0.014994601,-0.029755535,-0.02018957,0.0016644294,-0.0495594,-0.06895845,0.011532367,-0.023398368,0.04079106,0