08,0.015719576,-0.01013638,0.014153925,0.018720515,-0.01996384,-0.0036846462,0.030618375,0.016659576,-0.002166434,0.030282913,-0.0030292098,-0.008196306,0.017132249,0.021346664,0.004642707,0.019639483,-0.022478474,-0.01880144,-0.037606116,-0.011895408,-0.007047005,-0.0058810785,-0.01333506,-0.008842704,0.023992404,-0.02175565,0.0051750783,-0.0010478362,0.0032597918,0.0122041,0.0038196824,-0.005946904,0.006822477,0.011723365,-0.0055958177,0.006917819,0.0011962604,-0.009579867,0.038130753,-0.015898824,-0.013447662]","token_count":1061,"source_location":{"name":"Course 04 — Fluid Mechanics and River Hydraulics (with speaker notes).pptx","limitations":"Extracted slide XML text, table cell text and speaker notes. Images, diagrams, charts and embedded media are not visually interpreted; layouts are flattened.","extracted_end":71306,"extracted_start":68123},"created_at":"2026-11-18T08:06:29.161609+00:00"},{"id":"74522b52-c91f-41fc-ab61-dd22b67ae0b2","analysis_id":"47ea0217-a6c9-4726-984b-c2e788d4a5b7","chunk_index":17,"content":"hemically changes?\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n40\n1\nPump sizing needs total dynamic head and combined efficiencies, not only hydraulic output power.\n2\nConstruct static=5m and friction=10m at target Q\n3\ncalculate TDH\nWHY THIS HAPPENS\nA pump adds mechanical energy to fluid. The system requires static elevation head plus pipe friction and fittings; the pump supplies decreasing head with increasing flow. Their curve intersection determines a feasible operating point under assumptions.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 40]\nFirst, pump sizing needs total dynamic head and combined efficiencies, not only hydraulic output power.\nNext, construct static=5m and friction=10m at target Q.\nFinally, calculate TDH.\nThe sequence is a scientific explanation: the visible outcome follows from the preceding conditions, rather than appearing as an unexplained result.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 41]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  APPARATUS & OBSERVATION\nRAREMINDS\nConnect the science to real equipment and evidence\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n41\nRECONSTRUCTED TEACHING SCENE  •  NOT AUTHENTICATED FIELD FOOTAGE\nWHAT THE LEARNER MUST OBSERVE\nPump and system head curves with their intersection and correct power labels.\nHOW THE EVIDENCE IS PRODUCED\nInspect pump nameplate, rated curve, system elevation, pipe details and measured Q/H. Calculate hydraulic power first, then divide by efficiencies to estimate electrical demand.\nUse authentic method, equipment ID, calibration record and signed observations for a real laboratory result.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 41]\nPump and system head curves with their intersection and correct power labels.\nInspect pump nameplate, rated curve, system elevation, pipe details and measured Q/H. Calculate hydraulic power first, then divide by efficiencies to estimate electrical demand.\nThe pictured setup illustrates the relevant equipment or model. It is not authenticated footage from a completed measurement.\nA real result also depends on the specified method, equipment condition, calibration and identifiable source record.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 42]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 3  /  WORKING METHOD\nRAREMINDS\nFollow the process: input → action → observed result\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n42\n1\nSOURCE / SETUP\nConstruct static=5m and friction=10m at target Q\n2\nACTION / TRANSFER\ncalculate TDH\n3\nMEASUREMENT / CHANGE\nshow pump selection against Q-H curve\nVISIBLE RESULT / CAUTION: The hydraulic power is 2.94kW, smaller than required electrical input.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 42]\nThe source or setup is construct static=5m and friction=10m at target Q.\nThe calculation concerns TDH.\n","embedding":"[-0.0077545894,0.023627196,0.0030942105,-0.01092599,-0.013897144,-0.032923628,0.009248776,-0.030211488,-0.002839989,-0.08809376,0.008354926,0.024947166,0.020057917,-0.0010682632,0.0055956817,-0.013305053,0.017912041,-0.030893732,-0.0049013314,-0.00028866905,0.009003054,-0.0059580994,-0.0044458727,0.026077854,-0.06722994,0.0422682,0.010840666,-0.015168775,-0.028595788,0.10404538,-0.026410775,-0.019361533,-0.01925217,-0.021098228,0.028680809,0.02203793,2.9748412e-06,0.023299236,0.012280453,0.019267645,0.00952887,0.0008555664,-0.014943705,-0.0010000694,-0.0016784542,0.0035345822,-0.016338773,0.020071683,0.012353962,0.00903645,-0.015935108,-0.014820236,0.011799327,-0.0051516825,-0.012291476,-0.02203459,-0.021757739,0.021239951,0.028259594,0.006710894,-0.0145852,-0.009706644,0.022974689,0.024170956,-0.011622407,0.0037144343,0.03328878,-0.02103243,0.024214271,0.006097847,0.0046589836,-0.012114195,-0.0039968193,-0.0042205057,-0.0064932527,-0.04775495,-0.07204694,0.01789381,-0.014181703,0.031524017,0.0005743212,-0.022512086,-0.01032445,0.0023477261,-0.01874269,0.021912575,-0.042115096,-0.02415757,0.019988537,0.034396537,-0.0012321102,0.0035771576,-0.0027792933,-0.039553862,-0.013465404,-0.019774228,0.04584975,-0.02351866,-0.01626365,-0.015945803,-0.03699058,-0.015403611,0.0019984934,0.015044168,-0.0027111291,-0.022079233,-0.0018462804,0.0068312017,-0.014894304,0.02078167,-0.02391512,-0.20735425,0.0009626292,0.012726796,-0.032235645,0.03759257,0.023474662,0.0061141746,-0.012093669,0.0012352902,0.012815986,-0.0038615046,0.0030411682,-0.0076474054,-0.005060218,0.004096452,-0.014260497,-0.033762936,-0.0076836618,0.0014772672,0.02565084,0.021798002,-0.009313295,0.030842287