02,0.0036136527,-0.0049220123,-0.012285597,0.012583931,0.0076340083,-0.01587639,0.009846882,0.03141023,-0.03374672,-0.004941503,-0.043386117,-0.03417995,0.002964866,0.025489397,-0.016519869,0.0334408,0.012099104,-0.0013010717,-0.0074732048,-0.0015011476,0.01010625,-0.0121488,0.0018121522,-0.0037101596,0.008658139,-0.0131786475,-0.0044991216,0.016085096,0.00025140774,0.024472225,0.018889531,-0.027816396,0.034678306,0.011891153,-0.012225179,-0.00708182,-0.004991312,0.019982677,0.012206691,-0.02322,-0.04530817,-0.013057304,0.026942259,0.0050825994,0.009069395,-0.006566157,-0.009745788,0.0076636528,0.00908878,0.0026608403,0.01781488,-0.019118827,0.030472603,-0.017335879,-0.014536512,0.011202543,0.017215563,0.011359456,-0.020658093,0.006744003,-0.0025293815,0.0079133725,-0.009036158,-0.04017061,-0.014080733,-0.04510346,-0.032477397,-0.003540313,0.0026684327,0.012711119,0.020615496,0.009484372,0.002568828,-0.009973344,-0.02474668,0.0013933874,0.008059866,-0.010517545,-0.0027693945,0.012132243,-0.013454424,-0.013782811,-0.0051702973,-4.8517162e-05,-0.01180518,0.0061722193,-0.040939167,0.0056517255]","token_count":1067,"source_location":{"name":"Course 15 — Environmental Monitoring, Risk and Engineering Decisions (with speaker notes).pptx","limitations":"Extracted slide XML text, table cell text and speaker notes. Images, diagrams, charts and embedded media are not visually interpreted; layouts are flattened.","extracted_end":71348,"extracted_start":68147},"created_at":"2026-11-18T08:06:14.435833+00:00"},{"id":"da0ded6b-b4d7-43e8-b483-14dbdbc7c223","analysis_id":"61b722f5-8838-4257-8470-376c62f24aa4","chunk_index":22,"content":"y unqualified.  Unused budget does not authorise procurement or technical release.\nWHY THE ERROR MATTERS\nProcurement, technical approvals and public claims remain separately gated\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 49]\nThe incorrect claim is equating budget headroom with technical or procurement permission.\nHeadroom does not mean excluded work or procurement is approved; cheap action may be technically unqualified. Unused budget does not authorise procurement or technical release.\nThe error matters because it ignores this boundary: procurement, technical approvals and public claims remain separately gated.\nThe correction rests on the actual evidence and model, rather than on a rule remembered without its conditions.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 50]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 3  /  ACADEMIC GLOSSARY\nRAREMINDS\nRelated words and their precise meanings\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n50\nOption\nproposed action\nCost ceiling\navailable planning limit\nEligibility\nmethod/source support\nApproval\npermission to execute\nFeasibility\nevidence-based practicality\nApproval gate\nindependent release decision\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 50]\nThe term Option means proposed action.\nThe term Cost ceiling means available planning limit.\nThe term Eligibility means method/source support.\nThe term Approval means permission to execute.\nThe term Feasibility means evidence-based practicality.\nThe term Approval gate means independent release decision.\nThese definitions belong together because the model uses more than one quantity, structure or process. The words are precise scientific terms, not interchangeable labels.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 51]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 3  /  APPLY INDEPENDENTLY\nRAREMINDS\nNew case — answer before opening the next slide\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n51\nNEW SOURCE RECORD\nPlanning ceiling INR 120,000; six-option plan INR 98,000; conditional 