er notes for slide 68]\nThis different teaching case starts with plan INR90,000; conditional scope INR60,000; PO and invoice not issued.\nThe scientific question is: State outside conditional scope and paid amount if no ledger evidence is supplied.\nThe underlying principle is the same as in the taught example, but the data or conditions are different.\nA complete interpretation depends on the right relationship, consistent units, transparent calculation and a statement of what remains unknown. The result is explained on the following solution slide.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 69]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  COMPLETE SOLUTION\nRAREMINDS\nHow the new case is solved and checked\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n69\n1\nDifference=90000−60000\n2\nNo payment evidence is not evidence of zero paid.\nREASONED ANSWER\nINR30,000 outside conditional scope; paid = UNKNOWN pending verified ledger.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 69]\nThe new case is resolved by applying the earlier scientific relationship to the changed conditions.\nThe first calculation is difference=90000−60000.\nThe next calculation is no payment evidence is not evidence of zero paid.\nThe reasoned result is INR30,000 outside conditional scope; paid = UNKNOWN pending verified ledger.\nThis solution shows why the method works in a second situation, not just how to repeat the number from the first example.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 70]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  INDUSTRY APPLICATION\nRAREMINDS\nWhere this matters in engineering work\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n70\nRECONSTRUCTED TEACHING SCENE  •  NOT AUTHENTICATED FIELD FOOTAGE\nACTUAL JOB APPLICATION\nProject controls, procurement audit and case closure\nWHAT MAY BE REPORTED\n","embedding":"[0.005335483,0.01934931,0.008778717,-0.009444931,-0.014891669,-0.026208147,-0.0065459283,-0.06052075,0.009095206,-0.08371853,-0.0024546327,0.028102797,0.01444904,0.020120552,-0.011298714,-0.0142484605,0.016005503,-0.022466471,0.0076395436,-0.02907337,-0.025305495,-0.015634999,-0.022110518,0.014622388,-0.025508415,0.0025244362,0.00968473,-0.019326383,-0.03076968,0.10572724,0.01886375,-0.008611154,-0.018650455,0.0014618199,0.015825076,0.009389717,-0.008307539,0.00908448,0.009351365,0.015434605,0.0026916421,-0.029474586,0.023454208,-0.0048272638,0.0123414,-0.0020307242,0.017564632,0.021613374,-0.0042573973,0.0113982605,-0.01182163,-0.010636344,0.026245937,-0.02557919,0.023240259,-0.019566642,-0.026184024,0.028316328,0.05859389,0.007651303,-0.018073717,-0.0019213922,0.03332573,-0.0029722792,-0.007097648,-0.008405985,0.02696633,-0.027308302,0.00030822263,0.03114426,0.009518649,-0.002933449,-0.0123474,0.013178981,-0.01606187,-0.048054073,-0.08341775,0.037913267,-0.021280527,0.042321347,-0.0040693586,-0.013662789,-0.029799996,0.0066050333,-0.022297075,0.0068865605,-0.043643966,-0.026012518,0.028396966,0.047591466,-0.004568693,-0.03596864,0.011129571,-0.044586528,-0.031684384,-0.005554103,0.021938717,0.0009515278,-0.034477897,-0.05850314,-0.031230332,0.0024827428,-0.0069564898,0.0022267478,0.027267436,-0.0112679545,-0.012745439,0.01764057,0.028330497,0.009463514,-0.047985364,-0.19284728,-0.002022624,0.01488051,-0.028480953,0.038345665,0.04541373,0.009762978,-0.01495967,0.031522125,0.0110324,-0.006801591,-0.0027255826,-0.01899017,-0.04221688,-0.001847122,0.013373729,-0.01405753,-0.023477083,0.017037205,0.027946934,0.023063434,-0.0098084565,0.0061256257,-0.0036338393,-0.015949769,0.06618265,0.019222923,0.03621453,-0.019314835,0.0044184886,0.0017419273,0.017201109,-0.018073391,-0.035809323,-6