ndex":3,"content":"DS Course 4 source slide 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 8]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 1  /  WORKING METHOD\nRAREMINDS\nFollow the process: input → action → observed result\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n8\n1\nSOURCE / SETUP\nMeasure depth and velocity in three width bands\n2\nACTION / TRANSFER\ncalculate each A_i, Q_i\n3\nMEASUREMENT / CHANGE\ntotal Q=ΣQ_i\nVISIBLE RESULT / CAUTION: A single surface velocity is not an area-weighted mean discharge.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 8]\nThe measurement concerns depth and velocity in three width bands.\nThe calculation concerns each A_i, Q_i.\nThe observed or calculated outcome is total Q=ΣQ_i.\nA single surface velocity is not an area-weighted mean discharge.\nThis separates a visible scientific response from the further testing needed for a real operational conclusion.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 9]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 1  /  SOURCE RECORD\nRAREMINDS\nRead the values before calculating anything\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n9\nILLUSTRATIVE INPUTS — TAUGHT EXAMPLE\nThree 2m bands: depths 0.4,0.6,0.5m\nWORK STEP 1\nmean speeds .3,.4,.35m/s\nWORK STEP 2\nQ=.24+.48+.35=1.07m³/s\nBefore a real report is accepted, sample ID, date, method, unit and quality status must be checked.\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 9]\nThe given teaching inputs are Three 2m bands: depths 0.4,0.6,0.5m.\nThe first working relationship is mean speeds .3,.4,.35m/s.\nThe next calculation or interpretation is Q=.24+.48+.35=1.07m³/s.\nThe inputs and calculated steps are distinct. These figures are not presented as readings taken from a specific certified instrument.\nA field or laboratory report would additionally require an identifiable sample, method, date, units and quality status.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 4 source slide 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-1\n\n[Slide 10]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 04  /  LESSON 1  /  FORMULA & VARIABLES\nRAREMINDS\nBuild the scientific relationship from its parts\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n10\nQi=Ai vi; total Q=Σ(width_i×depth_i×velocity_i)\nCross-section area\nm²\nMean velocity\nm/s\nSegment width/depth\ngeometry\nDischarge Q\nm³/s\nMODEL LIMIT / ASSUMPTION:\nCurrent-meter calibration and safe site procedures required\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 10]\nThe scientific relationship is Qi=Ai vi; total Q=Σ(width_i×depth_i×velocity_i).\nIts symbols carry specific physical or chemical meanings and units. Changing the meaning of a variable changes what the equation can legitimately express.\nCross-section area means m².\nMean velocity means m/s.\nSegment width/depth means geometry.\n","embedding":"[-0.015077845,0.0037186716,0.00958841,-0.027491232,-0.017707046,-0.042407304,0.017127829,-0.060069002,-0.0011702052,-0.0758389,0.024632785,0.006374991,0.00095788646,0.029313749,-0.027769763,-0.010225768,0.0033889501,-0.0405563,-0.00901969,-0.0237411,0.039260145,-0.011432889,-0.03296416,0.024947708,-0.06414935,0.021484032,0.02597954,-0.02846277,-0.0217812,0.13460235,0.016294256,-0.029635089,-0.025281196,0.0036146946,0.02560448,0.005176262,0.0032883442,0.002165887,0.013761176,0.013209549,0.027197514,-0.044404022,-0.0071655265,0.0023935984,0.031185795,-0.0013331892,-0.00088695175,0.011239174,-0.006602482,0.008593838,-0.009337099,0.007318771,0.02318755,-0.0059470586,-0.0010886053,0.014395432,-0.015083883,0.011135462,0.037941184,0.0078582615,0.00625