,0.01403701,0.030443981,-0.01533387,0.0066178306,-0.00077393686,-0.009699827,0.020758586,-0.010506683,-0.0001772219,0.046833213,-0.03312173,0.0042855656,0.03420481,-0.004835518,0.0030569355,0.042478386,0.005033238,0.016693553,0.0055073216,0.015386097,0.024399268,0.008246411,-0.011476565,-0.02428249,-0.04162973,-0.011211446,-0.003824564,0.014203396,0.015762541,0.016811589,0.01388912,-0.012827767,0.00608143,0.0030955416,-0.0030854745,-0.003054135,-0.01606835,-0.013195312,0.016667267,-0.012476828,-0.011153799,-0.012040364,0.019114299,-0.023137093,0.013216849,-0.0050007408,0.0044977115]","token_count":1007,"source_location":{"name":"Course 04 — Fluid Mechanics and River Hydraulics (with speaker notes).pptx","limitations":"Extracted slide XML text, table cell text and speaker notes. Images, diagrams, charts and embedded media are not visually interpreted; layouts are flattened.","extracted_end":36981,"extracted_start":33962},"created_at":"2026-11-18T08:06:29.161609+00:00"},{"id":"f7715fc4-918c-4f25-ad71-363f8a7f1f09","analysis_id":"61b722f5-8838-4257-8470-376c62f24aa4","chunk_index":29,"content":"e of a payment record is not evidence that zero money was paid.\nCOMMON OVERCLAIM\nEntering zero where transaction evidence is absent; treating conditional approval as executed purchase\nPROFESSIONAL BOUNDARY\nAPP-04 states closure not authorised; learner cannot close case\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 65]\nA numeric budget remainder is not cash spent or available for purchasing without approvals. Absence of a payment record is not evidence that zero money was paid.\nA possible overclaim would be entering zero where transaction evidence is absent; treating conditional approval as executed purchase.\nThe professional limit is APP-04 states closure not authorised; learner cannot close case.\nA defensible conclusion says what the evidence establishes and does not silently extend it to an untested property or situation.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 66]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  ERROR ANALYSIS\nRAREMINDS\nFind the wrong reasoning and repair it\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n66\nINCORRECT OR MISLEADING CLAIM\nEntering zero in paid column when payment proof is missing.\nWHAT THE TAUGHT EVIDENCE REALLY SUPPORTS\nA numeric budget remainder is not cash spent or available for purchasing without approvals.  Absence of a payment record is not evidence that zero money was paid.\nWHY THE ERROR MATTERS\nAPP-04 states closure not authorised; learner cannot close case\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 66]\nThe incorrect claim is entering zero in paid column when payment proof is missing.\nA numeric budget remainder is not cash spent or available for purchasing without approvals. Absence of a payment record is not evidence that zero money was paid.\nThe error matters because it ignores this boundary: APP-04 states closure not authorised; learner cannot close case.\nThe correction rests on the actual evidence and model, rather than on a rule remembered without its conditions.\n[Sources]\nOriginal RAREMINDS Course 15 source slide 27, 28, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 34; teaching values are illustrative, not certified samples.\nhttps://www.epa.gov/risk\n\n[Slide 67]\nRAREMINDS  /  COURSE 15  /  LESSON 4  /  ACADEMIC GLOSSARY\nRAREMINDS\nRelated words and their precise meanings\nAll measurements on these pages are teaching examples unless an authenticated source is cited.\n67\nPlanned\nforecast cost\nConditional\nauthorised planning scope with conditions\nCommitted\nvalid PO/contract\nInvoiced\nbilled amount\nCommitment\npurchase obligation\nInvoice\nvendor claim\n\n[Speaker notes for slide 67]\nThe term Planned means forecast cost.\nThe term Conditional means authorised planning scope with conditions.\nThe term Committed means valid PO/contract.\nThe term Invoiced means billed amount.\nThe term Commitment means purchase obligation.\nThe term Invoice means vendor claim.\nThese definitions belong together because the model uses more than one quantity, structure or process. The words are precise scientific terms, not interchangeable labels.\n[Sources]\n","embedding":"[0.023044443,0.0064888024,-0.0010480148,-0.022221105,-0.023267873,-0.016888052,-0.015590176,-0.060396403,0.012032957,-0.082614176,-0.004667013,0.011935357,0.01382727,0.009438366,-0.017858151,-0.01291073,0.0071925363,-0.013630144,-0.0023207518,-0.012835574,-0.023216674,-0.0040313196,-0.012159664,0.024381222,-0.044354465,0.009034697,0.014986208,-0.018410077,-0.011841137,0.09581997,-0.006621245,-0.0015810723,-0.01034861,0.009892878,0.010517017,-0.007147926,0.0009028236,0.0051823617,0.023217354,0.04119403,-0.0029435272,-0.03160999,0.030797133,-0.0039219363,0.02441334,-0.0014722481,-0.006307254,0.014799594,-0.018794566,0.018784307,-0.020037638,-0.014378512,0.033894297,-0.019686999,0.03110773,-0.022218984,-0.0057314597,0.035735287,0.057517897,0.005311839,-0.005167414,0.0046917386,0.03494266,0.018012892,-0.01798733,-0.006017962,0.023099503,-0.015861169,0.015992364,0.0446026,0.019101253,-0.0028514548,-0.029521052,0.008286572,-0.008343998,-0.05475353,-0.09277079,0.024578374,-0.039334863,0.03058009,-0.015310271,0.0011847937,-0.027473593,0.022706466,-0.039669428,0.011085314,-0.037774608,-0.017578593,0.030196186,0.03308414,-0.008668862,-0.02905675,0.0044181,-0.03751742,-0.027509952,-0.007933234,0.0248836,-0.0012386277,-0.03414106,-0.039263114,-0.038069148,0.0044497335,-0.008840061,0.0056124376,0.018872898,-0.0017801374,-0.04791104,0.023267405,0.0056222463,0.026862195,-0.011737918,-0.16536272,-0.0056520845,0.015685009,-0.0201697,0.059911616,0.049080342,0.038907625,-0.01653046,0.021288691,0.010630216,-0.011925482,-0.024443615,-0.014967244,-0.028725643,0.00087493245,0.01831086,-0.013282846,-0.02342369,0.022727922,0.021797767,0.016809266,-1.4166995e-05,0.012967128,-0